{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9004db7c-8bdf-5c53-a892-e92c30054132",
    "name": "Querylab API (step 1)",
    "description": "Every endpoint the backend has after step 1: health, the current user, ask (text-to-SQL), saved LLM keys and allauth's headless (browser) API. Sign-in is Google or GitHub only.\n\n**Setup:** import this collection and `environment.json`, select the *Querylab local* environment,\n\n**CSRF:** run *Get CSRF cookie and current user* first. A collection test script copies the `csrftoken` cookie into `{{csrfToken}}` after every response (Django rotates it at login), and a collection pre-request script sends it as `X-CSRFToken` on every write.\n\n**Responses:** `/api/*` uses Querylab's envelope (`success`, `data`, ...; `/api/health` is unwrapped). `/_allauth/*` uses allauth's own shape (`status`, `data`, `meta`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Send the CSRF token on every write (Django checks it on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE).",
          "const unsafe = ['POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE'];",
          "const token = pm.environment.get('csrfToken');",
          "if (unsafe.includes(pm.request.method) && token) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-CSRFToken', value: token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Keep {{csrfToken}} in step with the csrftoken cookie (it rotates at login).",
          "const cookie = pm.cookies.get('csrftoken');",
          "if (cookie) pm.environment.set('csrfToken', cookie);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health and docs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every backend dependency: `querylab_app`, `querylab`, the read-only reader, Redis and the Huey worker. 200 with `status: ok`, or 503 with `status: degraded` and the failing check marked `fail`. Not wrapped in the envelope."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200, 503]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 503]));",
                  "pm.test('reports every check', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.keys('status', 'app_db', 'data_db', 'data_reader', 'redis', 'worker');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "OpenAPI schema",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/openapi.json",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "openapi.json"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The generated OpenAPI document for `/api/` (the interactive docs are at `/api/docs` in a browser)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200]));",
                  "pm.test('is OpenAPI', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('openapi'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Current user",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get CSRF cookie and current user (GET /api/me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Run this first.** Returns the signed-in user (200, envelope, with `providers`: `google` or `github`) or 401 when signed out. Either way it sets the `csrftoken` cookie, which the collection copies into `{{csrfToken}}` for every write."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200, 401]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 401]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.test('success envelope', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.equal(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('data');",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.test('returns the user', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.include.keys('id', 'email'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('error envelope', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.equal(false);",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.keys('success', 'status_code', 'message', 'code', 'errors');",
                  "  });",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('csrftoken cookie is set', () => pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('csrftoken')).to.equal(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
